<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- ========================================================================
     DROIDWORKS_PRIMITIVE_TIER_1 (packet B9). Jawa-fabricable counterparts to
     Parts_Droidworks.xml's 7 donor-grade parts, "at a grossly inferior
     level" (ruling 8) and "~40% of donor quality... the ladder tops out at
     'what you can find'" (§6 anti-exponential guardrail). Measured as: item
     Mass/MaxHitPoints/MarketValue set to 40% of the matching donor
     Standard-quality part's own values (Parts_Droidworks.xml), rounded to a
     sane whole number — the arithmetic a verify script can check without a
     live game (see the item file's own comparison table). Flammability
     left unscaled (not a "quality" axis).

     Ingredients are Steel + Wood only, NEVER ComponentIndustrial/
     ComponentSpacer — "Jawa-appropriate ingredients", the donor Frame's own
     recipe (Parts_Droidworks.xml) is the thing this tier is deliberately
     CHEAPER than. skillRequirements Crafting 1 (Crafting 2 on the Frame,
     matching Parts_Droidworks.xml's own Frame being the one part with real
     structural stakes) - a Jawa scavenger can bang these together without
     real expertise, which is the whole point of "very primitive".

     CompQuality kept on every part (same as the donor tier) for market-
     value flavor only: the install effect these parts grant
     (PartRecipes_Droidworks_Primitive.xml) is FLAT regardless of the
     rolled quality - see that file's own header for why (FOUNDRY's own
     call, option B of the item brief's two offered routes).
======================================================================== -->
